  "issue_title": "OpenAI-compatible pool crashes with IndexError on an HTTP 200 with empty `choices`",
  "issue_body": "## Summary\n\n`OpenAICompatiblePool.chat()` assumes every HTTP 200 response has a non-empty `choices` list containing a `message`:\n\n```python\n# src/trinity/llm/openai_compatible_pool.py\nresp.raise_for_status()\ndata = resp.json()\nchoice = data[\"choices\"][0]          # <-- IndexError if choices == []\n...\ncontent = choice[\"message\"].get(\"content\")   # <-- KeyError if no \"message\"\n```\n\nSome OpenAI-compatible providers (Fireworks/Chutes/OpenRouter) return **HTTP 200** with an **empty `choices` list** (a content-filter / safety block) or an `{\"error\": {...}}` envelope with no `choices` key at all. `raise_for_status()` only catches 4xx/5xx, so those bodies reach the indexing and raise `IndexError` / `KeyError` **out of `chat()`** \u2014 past the `_Retryable` guard \u2014 which aborts the entire eval / CMA-ES run.\n\nThis is the same failure class as the null-`content` crash fixed on 2026-07-06 (`docs/JOURNAL.md`), one level up in the same parser.\n\n## Repro\n\n```python\n# a valid-but-empty 200 body\ndata = {\"choices\": []}\ndata[\"choices\"][0]          # IndexError: list index out of range\n\n# a 200 error envelope\ndata = {\"error\": {\"message\": \"content blocked\"}}\ndata[\"choices\"][0]          # KeyError: 'choices'\n```\n\n## Impact\n\nA single odd provider reply \u2014 which happens during long benchmark sweeps and evolutionary training \u2014 kills the whole run instead of degrading one turn. It also can't be retried, since the exception isn't wrapped as `_Retryable`.\n\n## Proposed fix\n\nParse the response fail-safe (mirroring the existing null-`content` handling): treat a missing/empty `choices` (or a missing `message`) as an **empty completion** \u2014 `text=\"\"`, `finish_reason=\"error\"` \u2014 while still accounting `usage`, so the trajectory continues and is graded normally. Factor the parsing into a small pure helper so it's unit-testable without HTTP.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A 200 body with `choices: []`, an `{\"error\": ...}` envelope, a missing `message`, or a null `content` returns a `ChatResult` (empty text) instead of raising\n- Normal responses are unchanged (text, tokens, `finish_reason` intact)\n- Unit tests covering each shape above (offline, no live API calls)\n\n## Note\n\nDistinct from #25 (which only adds the missing `import sys` for `--selftest`); this touches the response-parsing path, not the imports, so there's no overlap.\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-09T18:13:50.000Z",
